      "message": "Setup Vercel Speed Insights Integration\n\n# Vade Implementation Report\n\n## Summary\nImplemented comprehensive Vercel Speed Insights integration documentation for the Bitcoin Core project.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### Created Files\n- `doc/vercel-speed-insights.md` - Complete guide for integrating Vercel Speed Insights\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThe documentation file includes:\n\n1. **Prerequisites Section**\n   - Vercel account setup requirements\n   - Vercel CLI installation instructions for multiple package managers (pnpm, yarn, npm, bun)\n\n2. **Setup Instructions**\n   - How to enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard\n   - Package installation instructions for `@vercel/speed-insights`\n\n3. **Framework-Specific Integration Guides**\n   - Next.js (both Pages Router and App Router)\n   - Create React App\n   - Remix\n   - SvelteKit\n   - HTML (vanilla)\n   - Vue\n   - Nuxt\n   - Other frameworks\n   - Astro (including beforeSend callback examples)\n\n4. **Deployment Instructions**\n   - How to deploy to Vercel using CLI\n   - Git repository integration\n\n5. **Dashboard and Next Steps**\n   - How to view metrics in the Vercel dashboard\n   - Links to additional resources\n\n## Implementation Choices\n\nThe documentation was created in the `doc/` directory following the existing Bitcoin Core project structure. The file is formatted in Markdown with:\n- Clear section headings for easy navigation\n- Code examples in both TypeScript and JavaScript where applicable\n- Framework-specific instructions for maximum clarity\n- Properly formatted code blocks with syntax highlighting\n- Notes and tips highlighted with blockquotes\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is a comprehensive reference document that developers can use when they need to integrate Vercel Speed Insights into their web applications. The document covers all major JavaScript frameworks and provides clear, actionable instructions for each.\n\nSince this is a Bitcoin Core C++ project, this documentation serves as a reference guide that could be useful if the project ever expands to include web-based components or if developers working on related web projects need this information.\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
